# models.env — THE place Edva's model ids are pinned.
#
# Read by:
#   shell  — `source "$ROOT/tools/agent/config/models.env"` (bash and zsh; plain
#            KEY=value lines, no expansion, no quotes — keep it that way)
#   node   — lib/models.cjs (parses this file; no second copy of an id)
#
# WHY ONE FILE. With the Opus id pinned in several separate code sites (the
# shared ephemeral runner, a job's own inline --model, the supervisor's web-read
# helper, a Q&A tool), a model bump is a grep-and-hope. Every Opus call site
# reads OPUS from here.
#
# WHAT IS NOT WIRED YET: SONNET is read only by the tools that already had an
# inline sonnet/opus map (daily-summary-review, day-statements). The resident
# supervisors (agent/config/agents.json) and ~40 per-invocation forks
# (hum harvesters, prechecks, *-run scripts, lib/*) still carry the id as
# a literal. All of them moved to claude-sonnet-5-5 together on 2026-10-06; a
# future bump must do the same (grep for the old id) and restart the supervisors.
#
# Changing a value: ephemeral forks re-read this file on every run, so a flip
# needs no restart. Verify first on Max from a GUI session, the same check as
# every previous bump:  claude -p --model <id> --effort xhigh  → returns OK.
# Pricing for the cost tools lives with the cost tools (edva-cost-report,
# edva-allowance-coverage, cost-review-prefetch); add the new id's rates there.

# Opus tier — ephemeral launchd forks (run-ephemeral-opus.sh and its callers,
# and the installation's own fork triggers), web-read, daily-summary-review
# (its DEFAULT reviewer and repairer), and the opus escalation
# tier of day-statements.
# 2026-10-06: claude-opus-5 -> claude-opus-5-5 ($4/$20 per Mtok, cache read $0.20).
EDVA_MODEL_OPUS=claude-opus-5-5

# Sonnet tier — see "WHAT IS NOT WIRED YET" above before changing.
# 2026-10-06: claude-sonnet-5 -> claude-sonnet-5-5 (same $2/$10, cache read $0.20),
# together with every supervisor in agents.json and the hard-coded call sites.
EDVA_MODEL_SONNET=claude-sonnet-5-5
